                    "fillColor": "#a3adbd",
                    "fillOpacity": 1
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Arimo",
                "text": "A hold that clears a track fills the held pedal's LED pill: red grows from both ends toward the centre over the long-press time (800 ms by default), and the track clears when the ends meet. Releasing early, a mode change or a lost link ends the fill at once and the pill shows its normal state; after the clear it shows the empty-track state. The app streams the progress every 20 ms in the optional CLEAR_HOLD message (console firmware 2.6, protocol still 12, so older firmware shows no fill and nothing wrong). No screen mirrors the LED pill: Tracks draws no pedals, and the Custom face's Pending Hold bar already times the same hold."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
            "textAlign": "left",
            "fontId": "custom-99a2c890-1804-450c-8af8-6b60ee9a6b27",
            "fontSize": "24",
